    "customfield_12311020": null,
    "customfield_12313320": "<div style='font-weight:bold;color:red;text-align:center'>This project has a <a href=\"https://lucene.apache.org/core/discussion.html\">user mailing list and an IRC channel</a> for support. If you are looking for support, or if you are not sure whether the behavior that you are observing is expected or not, please discuss it there first.</div>",
    "customfield_12314134": null,
    "duedate": null,
    "customfield_12314132": null,
    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12466366/comment/12912325",
          "id": "12912325",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=ryantxu",
            "name": "ryantxu",
            "key": "ryantxu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ryan McKinley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "If we chance the jar file names from -dev to -SNAPSHOT, the same build can be easily integrated with a maven snapshot repository (and tested -- LUCENE-2268).\n\nI'd like to avoid a discussion about the odities of maven, but lets just take as a given that if the artifact is named \"-SNAPSHOT\" then eveytime you use it, it makes sure it is the most recent version.  To be able to test (or have a real SNAPSHOT repository) we will either have to:\n  1. rename the .jar to -SNAPSHOT\n  2. run ant twice, once with the current -dev settings, then again with -Ddev.verrsion=4.0-SNAPSHOT\n\nIn my book, the aesthetic loss of \"-dev\" is worth the gain to let the maven community use (and test!) snapshot builds.  This also greatly simplifies building a test case for our maven files (LUCENE-2268)\n\nThoughts?  Objections?  \n\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=ryantxu",
            "name": "ryantxu",
            "key": "ryantxu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ryan McKinley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2010-09-20T03:56:53.028+0000",
          "updated": "2010-09-20T03:56:53.028+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12466366/comment/12912491",
          "id": "12912491",
          "author": {
